# Backend Rules

## Security
- NEVER expose GROQ_API_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY, or SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to frontend
- All AI and email routes MUST verify JWT via verifyAndLimit()
- Dev bypass (local-dev-token) only in development

## API Design
- All routes return JSON with { ok: true, data } or { error: "message" }
- Always handle OPTIONS for CORS preflight
- Use try/catch on all async handlers — never let unhandled rejections crash server

## Supabase
- Use getSupabase() lazy init pattern (not module-level createClient)
- Service role client only on server — never import in App.tsx
- Rate limit email_generation and card_scan via increment_ai_usage RPC

## Email
- Use Resend API first (RESEND_API_KEY)
- SMTP fallback if GMAIL_USER + GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD set
- Dev log fallback if neither configured
- Never fail silently — always log email errors

## Reminder Engine
- Uses setInterval(1 hour) — do not block with await at top level
- Mark reminder_done=true after sending to prevent duplicate emails
- Handle Supabase errors gracefully — log and continue

## New Routes
- Add to server.js with clear comment block
- Add to docs/ARCHITECTURE.md route table
- Add to docs/TEST_PLAN.md API section
